course: dictionary
lesson: 11315
title: Yes, and all its faces
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Yes» is a small word with many jobs. Most of the time it means you agree or accept: «Yes, please» means you would like the thing you are offered. Read the words around it to find out which job it is doing.
explain: «The Queen asks Alice if she can play croquet: «Yes!»» Here yes is an answer. It is a short, happy agreement, and the exclamation mark shows how it is said. Check the meaning by putting your idea into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Yes can also be a shout, as in «Yes! We won!», or a noun, as in «Her answer was a clear yes.» Sarcasm flips the meaning: «Oh yes, very clever» means you think the person was not clever at all.
fact: Yes is most often used to agree, accept or say that something is true.
fact: Casual words for yes include yeah, yep, yup, sure and deffo (UK, meaning definitely).
fact: Formal words for yes include affirmative, indeed and certainly.
fact: Sea lions learn to open their mouths for vet checks when a trainer's whistle says «yes, that's right», and a fish follows.
fact: In Russian and Ukrainian, tak means yes, and ne tak means «not like that» or wrong.
exercise: The Queen asks Alice if she can play croquet. Alice shouts «Yes!» What does yes mean here? | * I can play | I am the winner | Goodbye | I am the Queen
exercise: «Oh yes, very clever,» said Sam after the spill. What does Sam really mean? | Yes, I accept your gift | I agree you were very clever | * I think you were not clever at all | I am calling you over
exercise: Which word is a casual way to say yes? | Affirmative | Certainly | * Yep | Indeed
test: Which word means yes in a formal way? | Yup | Yeah | * Affirmative | Sure
test: In «Her answer was a clear yes.», what job does yes do? | * A noun | A number | An adjective | A verb
exam: «Respond in the affirmative or the negative.» What does this instruction ask you to do? | * Answer yes or no, with a clear reply | Write a long story | Ask a new question | Shout your name
